25
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.590
Colony for Epileptics opened at Cambridge in 1925. Over time

26
00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.310
these places shifted from education to lifelong custodial care, and

27
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.970
by the 1960s they were overcrowded and understaffed.

28
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.640
Then there are the eugenics laws. A 1917 law let

29
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.000
county probate judges commit people judged feeble minded without their

30
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.020
families' consent. Being poor or behaving unusually could count as

31
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.480
a sign. A 1925 law authorized sterilization.

32
00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:41.670
At least 2,204 Minnesotans were sterilized between 1925 and 1945,

33
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.210
77% of them women, and the true number is unknown,

34
00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.170
because no central board kept records.

35
00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.760
What struck me is that the people behind this saw

36
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.980
themselves as reformers. The module's lesson is not that reform

37
00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.940
